@startuml
title find_me_in_wood — LNP/2: explicit link switching by PROPOSE / ACCEPT (no fallback)
autonumber
participant "A" as A
participant "B" as B

== 1. Offers and first link (inside encrypted, signed beacons) ==
A ->> B : BT beacon {offers=[BT, WD, SMS(+380..A)]}
B ->> A : BT beacon {offers=[BT, SMS(+380..B)]}
A ->> B : BT beacon {prop=[B: BT, e=1]}
B -> B : BT offered by both -> link(A)=BT
B ->> A : BT beacon {acc=[A: BT, e=1]}
A -> A : link(B)=BT

== 2. Weak link: propose over a channel that still works ==
note over A : missed a beacon from B on BT
A ->> B : beacon {prop=[B: SMS, e=2]}\n(over weak BT or relayed by C)
B -> B : link(A)=SMS
B ->> A : beacon {acc=[A: SMS, e=2]}
A -> A : link(B)=SMS
A ->> B : SMS "FMIW1:..." position report (every 30 min, max 10/h)

== 3. Nothing gets through: no switch ==
note over A, B : proposal repeated on 3 beacons, unanswered -> expires;\nlink stays as it was, nobody is texted

== 4. Back on a cheaper radio ==
B ->> A : BT beacon (direct)
A ->> B : BT beacon {prop=[B: BT, e=3]}
B ->> A : BT beacon {acc=[A: BT, e=3]}
note over A, B : link = BT on both, SMS reports stop
@enduml
